Homepage: https://zexplore.ca

Package: zexplore
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, bash, zfsutils-linux | zfs
Recommends: fzf, pv, mbuffer, python3
Suggests: libvirt-clients
Description: A direct interface to your ZFS primitives — not a dashboard
 zexplore is a fast, keyboard-driven console for OpenZFS: browse datasets and
 snapshots with a full properties + permissions view, snapshot on tap, point-
 and-shoot replicate over SSH, explore files inside datasets/snapshots/zvols,
 and a scoped snapshot/rollback transaction API. Every action is a plain
 zfs/zpool command — a primitives tool, not a dashboard.
